---
const title = 'The Build Log | BitBrd';
const description = 'A running, dated journal of real work on real local businesses. Written by the person doing the work, as it happens.';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
<title>{title}</title>
<meta name="description" content={description} />
<link rel="canonical" href="https://bitbrd.com/log" />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Press+Start+2P&family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
<style>
:root{--navy-900:#082545;--navy-800:#0A1F3D;--sky:#9FD4F2;--sky-light:#CFE9F7;--ink:#0A1628;--cream:#F7FAFD;--text:#E8F2FC;--muted:#8CA3BA;--green:#34D399;--border:rgba(159,212,242,0.15)}
*{margin:0;padding:0;box-sizing:border-box}
body{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;background:var(--ink);color:var(--text);line-height:1.65}
.wrap{max-width:820px;margin:auto;padding:60px 24px 80px}
.eyebrow{font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:10px;color:var(--sky);letter-spacing:0.15em;text-transform:uppercase}
h1{font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:clamp(1.1rem,3vw,1.7rem);color:var(--cream);margin:16px 0 14px;line-height:1.5}
.lede{color:var(--muted);max-width:60ch;margin-bottom:14px}
.lede b{color:var(--text)}
.rule{height:1px;background:var(--border);margin:34px 0 0}

.entry{display:grid;grid-template-columns:128px 1fr;gap:28px;padding:34px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
.entry-date{font-family:'Press Start 2P',monospace;font-size:9px;color:var(--green);line-height:1.9;padding-top:5px}
.entry-date span{display:block;color:var(--muted);font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;font-size:0.76rem;letter-spacing:0.04em;margin-top:4px}
.entry h2{font-size:1.12rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--cream);margin-bottom:0.6rem;line-height:1.4}
.entry p{color:var(--muted);font-size:0.95rem;margin-bottom:0.6rem;max-width:62ch}
.entry p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
.entry b{color:var(--text)}
.entry a{color:var(--sky);border-bottom:1px dotted rgba(159,212,242,0.4)}
.entry a:hover{color:var(--sky-light);border-bottom-style:solid}
a{text-decoration:none;color:inherit}

.foot{margin-top:40px;display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;padding:13px 22px;font-weight:600;font-size:0.9rem;border-radius:5px;text-decoration:none}
.btn-p{background:var(--sky);color:var(--navy-900)}
.btn-p:hover{background:var(--sky-light)}
.btn-g{border:1px solid rgba(159,212,242,0.35);color:var(--sky)}
.btn-g:hover{border-color:var(--sky)}
@media(max-width:640px){.entry{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:8px}.entry-date{display:flex;gap:12px;align-items:baseline}.entry-date span{margin-top:0}}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
  <span class="eyebrow">BitBrd &middot; the build log</span>
  <h1>What we actually shipped this week.</h1>
  <p class="lede">A running journal of real work on real local businesses, written by me as it happens. No schedule, no ghostwriter. Entries land when something ships. <b>Newest first.</b></p>
  <div class="rule"></div>

  <article class="entry">
    <div class="entry-date">JUN 11<span>2026</span></div>
    <div>
      <h2>The skyline took twelve tries</h2>
      <p>Two evenings on the pixel New Orleans skyline at the bottom of our homepage. The St.&nbsp;Louis Cathedral alone went through <b>five drawings</b>, each one traced against a photograph of the real building and argued over tower by tower. At one point there were square clouds. We don't speak of the square clouds.</p>
      <p>The whole rejected-version trail is posted on <a href="/drafts">the cutting room floor</a>. The engineering story is at <a href="/skyline">/skyline</a>: the entire animated scene weighs 3.3&nbsp;KB, smaller than one emoji image.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <div class="entry-date">JUN 10<span>2026</span></div>
    <div>
      <h2>663 pages for a trophy shop</h2>
      <p>Rebuilt <a href="https://www.artrophies.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discount Trophies of Arkansas</a>, a shop that has been engraving since 1978. Their catalog export became <b>663 fast product pages</b> overnight.</p>
      <p>One wrinkle I liked: trophy pricing depends on engraving, so they don't print prices. Instead of a cart, the site has a quote basket. Pick your items, send the list, get a real quote from a real person. The site works the way the shop works, not the other way around.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <div class="entry-date">JUN 10<span>2026</span></div>
    <div>
      <h2>West Little Rock Glass, round two</h2>
      <p>Five new service pages for <a href="https://westlittlerockglass.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">WLRG</a>: shower doors, mirrors, storefront glass and more, each one written to answer what someone actually types into Google at 7am with a broken window. Plus 301 redirects so the old links don't die.</p>
      <p>Tested the quote form myself before telling them it works. It works.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <div class="entry-date">MAY<span>2026</span></div>
    <div>
      <h2>The kitchen screen and the tarot system</h2>
      <p>Built Witches Brew a custom kitchen display: new orders pop onto an iPad behind the bar within seconds of hitting the register, color-coded by how long they've been waiting. It replaced a <b>$228/year</b> subscription and runs on a small computer at the shop. No cloud, no monthly fee, no outage when the internet hiccups.</p>
      <p>The part I'm proudest of rides on the same system: <b>a tarot draw with your order</b>. Nothing like it has been done in a caf&eacute; before. A tarot card comes out with your drink; scan it, and your card reveals itself on the shop's site. It feels personal to the business because it is. Happy customers get a nudge toward a Google review and the loyalty list. Unhappy ones get routed straight to the owners' inbox instead of a public one-star. Connection, reviews, and feedback, all from one little card.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <div class="entry-date">APR 15<span>2026</span></div>
    <div>
      <h2>West Little Rock Glass, round one</h2>
      <p>A custom glass shop with two decades of work behind it, stuck on an old site whose pages were literally named <b>/blank-1</b>. Round one rebuilt the whole thing: new homepage, all eight services, real photos of their actual work, and a testimonial from a real customer in her own words.</p>
      <p>Loads in a blink on a job-site phone, which is where their customers are standing when they search.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="entry">
    <div class="entry-date">JAN&ndash;MAY<span>2026</span></div>
    <div>
      <h2>Witches Brew, the long arc</h2>
      <p>Website, local SEO, phone system, and a custom dashboard for a brand-new coffee shop in Mid-City New Orleans, up against the French Quarter's established caf&eacute;s. Monthly revenue went <b>$10K &rarr; $30K in five months</b>; the owners check the dashboard every morning before the first pour.</p>
      <p>Full numbers in the <a href="/#case-studies">case study</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="foot">
    <a class="btn btn-p" href="/#contact">Want on this list? &rarr;</a>
    <a class="btn btn-g" href="/">&larr; Back to BitBrd</a>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
